### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________
ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION BUILDING CHEYENNE’S FUTURE BY REAFFIRMING
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE’S COMMITMENT TO ETHICAL PRINCIPLES AND
EFFICIENCY IN GOVERNMENT”
WHEREAS,    The City of Cheyenne continues to face ongoing budgetary pressures due
to multiple factors including the recent recession, increased fixed costs, geographic growth, and
reduced funding from other levels of government, thereby increasing the need for the operations
of City government to be efficient, effective, and deliver the most value possible to citizens; and

WHEREAS, The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne recognizes that these
budgetary constraints necessitate that the City of Cheyenne take action to improve how it does
business in an effort to spur economic development and increase City revenues as a result; and

WHEREAS,   The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne strives to improve and adapt
to current conditions and remain ethically sound; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne desires to hold the highest
ethical standards and transparency possible in all its dealings, and furthermore, recognizes the
value in a partnership with its citizens to achieve such,

WHEREAS, The Greater Cheyenne Chamber of Commerce has taken an interest in
helping the City of Cheyenne improve by adopting its “Building Cheyenne’s Future Strategy
Document,” and

WHEREAS,  The Greater Cheyenne Chamber of Commerce and other community
stakeholders have offered suggestions regarding how the City can better improve the service it
provides to its citizenry; and

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING, THAT:

The Governing Body supports the administration’s efforts to revise and update the City’s
personnel policies to address, among other topics, the following:

-rules related to gifts;

-rules regarding advocacy before the Governing Body; and

-rules against retaliatory behavior against private industry; and

In addition, the Mayor shall develop and propose to the Governing Body, together with the
Mayor's proposed annual operating budget ordinance for fiscal year 2016, a formal complaint
and resolution process in regard to citizens who take issue with City governance to heighten
transparency and fairness in order to decrease any perception that whistleblowers would be
subject to retaliation.
```

